{"type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn8le06ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn8le06ob10re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn8le06ob10re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn8le06ob10re2img01.jpg", "text": "In a busy, active society like ours, many services are made available 24 hours a day. Nurses, doctors, factory workers, cashiers in 24-hour stores, all ought to spend long nights each month working while most of the city sleeps. What many people do not realize is that working at night could do more than simply make you tired.", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn8le06ob10re2img02.jpg", "text": "A research study was recently done on hospital nurses in the U.S. The nurses in the study were supposed to work several nights every month in addition to their regular day and evening work. What was discovered was that these nurses had a 70 percent higher chance of having a heart attack than people who work regular hours.", "id": 2, "time": "20200"}, {"image": "engenn8le06ob10re2img03.jpg", "text": "The reason for the increase in the risk of heart attack has to do with stress hormones. When people work at the time they should be resting, the body produces a chemical that proceeds to make them feel stress. In time, these chemicals, called stress hormones, can damage the heart.", "id": 3, "time": "38000"}, {"image": "engenn8le06ob10re2img03.jpg", "text": "It may be necessary to work nights in our society, but what about the people who risk their health serving us? We had better find a way to lower the health risks but still enjoy our night-time services.", "id": 4, "time": "53000"}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about jobs, work