uiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0, "correct": 0, "selected": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 1, "correct": 1, "selected": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "RSLT", "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Tales from the Workplace", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Cost of Working at Night", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 6, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people's backgrounds in a wider variety of communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Using Modals to Add Meaning", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modal verbs to add meaning to the main verb of a sentence. <br/> They help to provide a clearer picture or context to the reader or listener.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Some examples of modals are: <span class=\"italic\">should</span>, <span class=\"italic\">had better</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">supposed to</span>.<br/>This group of modals add the meanings of advice, obligation or necessity.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They come before the main verb of the sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the following chart with examples of each modal. Practice reading the examples aloud.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Should</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Advice\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">When people work at the time they should be resting, the body produces a chemical that proceeds to make them feel stress.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Ought to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Advice\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Nurses, doctors, factory workers, all ought to spend long nights each month working.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Had better</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Strong Advice <br/>(Necessity)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We had better find a way to lower the health risks but still enjoy our night-time services. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Supposed to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Obligation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The nurses in the study were supposed to work several nights every month in addition to their regular day.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Notice the reduction of <span class=\"italic\">had better</span>. In speaking, it is normally reduced to <span class=\"italic\">'d better</span>.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Gerunds and Infinitives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>A <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> is a verb ending with <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> (<span class=\"italic\">doing</span>).<br/>An <span class=\"strong\">infinitive</span> is <span class=\"italic\">to</span> + verb (<span class=\"italic\">to do</span>).</p>There are rules about which verbs you can use with gerunds and which verbs you can use with infinitives.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Verbs commonly followed by a gerund:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Verbs that express <span class=\"strong\">likes/dislikes</span>:<ul><li>like</li><li>love</li><li>enjoy</li><li>dislike</li><li>hate</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"italic\">Tom <span class=\"strong\">disliked confronting</span> people about money. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The verbs <span class=\"italic\">like</span>/<span class=\"italic\">love</span>/<span class=\"italic\">hate</span> can also be followed by an infinitive.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Some other verbs that are followed by a gerund:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>anticipate</li><li>consider</li><li>delay</li><li>complete</li><li>involve</li><li>suggest</li><li>risk</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use gerunds after prepositions:<br/><span class=\"italic\">These nurses had a 70 percent higher chance <span class=\"strong\">of having</span> a heart attack.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These are some verbs that are followed by an infinitive:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>hope</li><li>proceed</li><li>seem</li><li>need</li><li>happen</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"italic\">The body produces a chemical that <span class=\"strong\">proceeds to make</span> them feel stress.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use infinitives after adjectives. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"italic\">It may be <span class=\"strong\">necessary to work</span> nights in our society.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What was discovered was that these nurses had a 70 percent higher chance of having a heart attack than people who work regular hours.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When people work at the time they should be resting, the body produces a chemical that proceeds to make them feel stress. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It may be necessary to work nights in our society, but what about the people who risk their health serving us?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "active", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having energetic activity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In a busy, active society like ours, we are awake day and night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about work and health.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "service ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a system supplying a public need", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Many services are available day and night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "24 hours a day", "type": "name"}, {"content": "all day; around the clock", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In a busy, active society like ours, many services are made available 24 hours a day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "24-hour", "type": "name"}, {"content": " open or available all day and all night", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Nurses, doctors, factory workers, cashiers in 24-hour stores work while the rest of us sleep.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "heart attack", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a sudden, sometimes serious, malfunction of a part of the heart muscle", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What was discovered was that these nurses had a 70 percent higher chance of having a heart attack than people who work regular hours.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hormone ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a substance produced in tissue fluids such as blood to stimulate specific cells or tissues", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The reason for the increase in the risk of heart attack has to do with stress hormones.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le06ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "On the Internet, read about these jobs: firefighter, hospital nurse, fisherman, taxi driver, high school teacher.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make some notes on the responsibilities of people who do these jobs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Put the jobs in order from most stressful (1) to least stressful (5). Be prepared to explain your choices.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, compare lists and discuss any differences.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about jobs, work and staying healthy.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about my attitudes toward an action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about what I should, ought to, had better, or am supposed to do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about stressful jobs and decide which are the most stressful.", "type": "text"}]}]}